-- title:
--   Galois model over K(j) with ramification dividing 6 in characteristic 3
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer (carrying a `NeZero` assumption), $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ a subgroup, and assume $3 \nmid M$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$, and let $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of those elements of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose associated unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ under `gamma0Units` lies in $H$. Inside the Laurent series field $K((q))$ consider `qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`, the subfield generated over $K$ by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of a common weight $k$ on $\Gamma$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ and the reduction of $p_g$ is nonzero. Let $x$ be an element of that field whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC K`, the reduction to $K$ of $q^{-1}\cdot E_4^3\eta^{-24}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$. The assertion is the existence of a field $L$ in the same universe as $K$, a $K$-algebra structure on $L$, and a $K$-algebra homomorphism $\iota$ from `qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ` to $L$, such that $L$ is a finite-dimensional Galois extension of the subfield $K(\iota x)$ generated by $\iota x$, and such that every place $P$ of $L$ over $K$ (a proper valuation subring of $L$ containing $K$ which is a principal ideal ring) with $\mathrm{ord}_P(\iota x) > 0$ satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_P(\iota x) \mid 6$.
--
--   This provides a Galois model, in characteristic $3$, of the covering $X_H(M) \to X(1)$: the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(M)$ modulo $3$ is embedded in a finite Galois extension of the rational function field $K(j)$, with all ramification indices above the point $j = 0$ dividing $6$, the bound reflecting the automorphisms of an elliptic curve with $j = 0$ in characteristic $3$. It is used in the ramification and genus estimates for modular curves in characteristic $3$, in particular by [`ModularCurve.hasseRootFn_notMem_x1FunctionFieldC_charThree`](thm.html#ModularCurve.hasseRootFn_notMem_x1FunctionFieldC_charThree), [`ModularCurve.ord_dvd_twelve_div_sub_one_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_dvd_twelve_div_sub_one_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC_of_lt_five) and [`ModularCurve.two_mul_index_le_sum_ordDiff_D_add_natCard_doubleCoset_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.two_mul_index_le_sum_ordDiff_D_add_natCard_doubleCoset_of_lt_five).
